items: serve-binds-all-interfaces
paths: file:v1/runtime/backend/rust/src/main/resources/scalascript/rust-runtime/HttpRs file:v1/runtime/http-server/jvm/src/main/scala/scalascript/server/jvm/JdkServerBackend.scala file:v1/runtime/http-server/jvm-fast/src/main/scala/scalascript/server/jvm/fast/FastServerBackend.scala file:v2/runtime/std/http-fast-plugin/src/main/scala/ssc/plugin/httpfast/NioNativeHttpServerHost.scala file:tests/e2e/http-bind-address-gate.sh file:.github/workflows/ci.yml file:INBOX.md file:BUGS.md
scope: |
  `serve(port)` could not be told where to bind, so every .ssc service was LAN-reachable. Measured
  with lsof, the lanes also disagreed with each other: run 127.0.0.1, --v1 `*`, build-rust `*`.
  SSC_HTTP_BIND is now read by all three (TLS paths included) and an unresolvable value stops the
  server. Each lane KEEPS its default — changing one is a product decision, filed with the
  measurement. Gate reads the socket from lsof, not from a log line.
next: gate wired in ci.yml, entries, then land
